  "limitations": [
    "SCHED-02 owns exclusive active claim acquisition. SCHED-03 consumes and transactionally fences an already issued schedule ID, due instant, owner, claim time, expiry, recurrence version, and fencing version tuple.",
    "Restart proof deliberately resubmits the same committed occurrence while its claim remains active. SCHED-06 owns expired-lease discovery, restart recovery, and recovery races.",
    "SCHED-04 owns grace calculation and skip or run_once misfire behavior. SCHED-03 processes the normal claimed occurrence anchored to the persisted due instant.",
    "SCHED-03 atomically persists the occurrence, WorkItem, primary Run, initial transition, and receipt audit. SCHED-05 owns recurrence recomputation, next-run advancement, occurrence audit, and lease release in the larger atomic transaction.",
    "Mode, campaign-brief reference, instance configuration revision, and payload come from a trusted schedule input mapper and are revalidated here; schedule source, event, instance, trigger, and workflow bindings cannot be caller-selected.",
    "Stable IDs and uniqueness provide idempotent receipt identity, not authorization or exactly-once Run execution.",
    "Runtime tests use file-backed SQLite. PostgreSQL table and constraint DDL compile, but PostgreSQL runtime contention and migrations are not exercised.",
    "Worker polling, public APIs, authorization, scheduler metrics, recurrence upgrades, and deployment remain outside this requirement."
